WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.320
- [Instructor] So, we are asked,

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:04.060
question mark is roughly equal

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.500
to this squiggly equal
sign right over here,

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.140
this means roughly equal to,

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.310
so not exactly equal to

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.920
44 times 78.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.700
So one way to think about
it is, 44 times 78 is

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.170
roughly equal to what?

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.150
So they're really asking us to estimate.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.600
So I encourage you to pause this video

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.500
and try to think through
how you would estimate

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.300
what 44 times 78 is.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.990
Once again, you don't
have to get it exactly,

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.680
you just want to get it roughly.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.274
And think about which of these choices

00:00:32.274 --> 00:00:35.823
are closest to that estimation of yours.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.470
All right now, let's
work through it together.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.627
So for me, the best way to
estimate is to think about,

00:00:41.627 --> 00:00:43.547
"Hey, can I think of these numbers,

00:00:43.547 --> 00:00:44.757
"can I estimate these numbers,

00:00:44.757 --> 00:00:46.950
"or think about what are
they roughly equal to?"

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.700
And when I think about what
they're roughly equal to I want

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.140
to think about numbers that are easy

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.390
to multiply potentially in my head.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.580
So for example 44 is
reasonably close to 40,

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.507
so I could say that,

00:00:57.507 --> 00:01:02.507
"Hey this is approximately
equal to or roughly equal to 40,

00:01:03.837 --> 00:01:07.850
"so that's my estimate of
44, or 44 is roughly 40."

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.097
And then 78 I could say,

00:01:09.097 --> 00:01:12.317
"Hey, that's pretty close
to 80" and so I could say,

00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:16.860
"This is roughly equal to 40 times 80,"

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.530
and this is pretty straight forward.

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.230
Some of you might already recognize

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:23.390
that four times eight is 32,

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:26.900
and then we have four tens
and then we have eight tens,

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.070
so it would be four times
eight times 10 twice.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.440
But if what I just said
is confusing to you,

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.430
we could think about it this way.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.890
40 times 80 is the same
thing as four times 10,

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.750
that's 40, times eight
times 10, that's 80,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.470
and this is equal to, I'm just
gonna switch the order here

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:47.450
of this multiplication which we can do,

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:52.040
this is equal to four times
eight times 10 times 10,

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.040
four times eight is 32,

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.490
10 times 10 is 100.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.710
So we can say that this
is equal to 32 hundreds,

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.470
or we could view that as 3,200,

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.780
which we could also view as 32 hundreds.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.980
And so that is this
choice right over here.

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.260
Now this isn't exactly
what 44 times 78 is,

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:14.950
but it's roughly, and this is useful.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.640
Sometimes in life, you just
have to get a rough sense

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.510
of what something is going to be.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.200
Sometimes when you even are
trying to find this exact

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.580
product, your brain wants to
check does that make sense?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.450
Let say you went through some
process to figure out this,

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.040
and you got some number

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.110
that is close to 20, and you're
like, "Wait, wait a minute"

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.890
But roughly when I
think about 40 times 80,

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.410
this should be close to 3,200,

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.960
I must have done something wrong.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.623
So it also helps you
keep a check on yourself.

